  "_provenance": [
    "Vendored from chant packages/core/src/terraform/aws-resources.ts (AWS_CARVE_TYPES), the hand-curated AWS carve-out table for chant's carve advisor and carve emit (issue #43, tools/mapping-gen).",
    "chant is a sibling checkout at ../chant relative to this repo's parent, not a dependency of this repo; this file is a data transcription, not an import.",
    "78 entries transcribed by hand on 2026-08-12, one per AWS_CARVE_TYPES array element, in source order. identityAttr is null for the 27 entries whose chant row carries none.",
    "Consumed by the row generator (a separate issue in this batch), not by mapping-gen's own join; it travels with the mapping artifact because both are keyed by tf_type.",
    "Adjudicated 2026-08-14 (#100): deliberate curation, almost fully retired by sharper sources. row-gen consults this file LAST among argument-name sources (identity schema, then import grammar, then this; tools/row-gen/classify.go resolveArgName), and a full proposal run attributes exactly ONE argument to it today: aws_ecs_cluster's \"name\", where the 6.59.0 provider serves no identity schema and the import grammar composes nothing. It goes stale in one direction only - every provider release that adds an identity schema for a seeded type retires that entry silently - and it is invalidated for a type the moment live/survey-full.json carries required_for_import for it. When the aws_ecs_cluster entry retires, delete this file and the carveseed.go loader with it."
  ],
